commit 6c4fff53e86c87dbdec62e828765697db04068a3

C03: the answer to «what music?» grounds the playback query on the completed request, and a bracket inside an observed title is not a placeholder (MUSIC1573)

MUSIC1571 (executed, not adjudicable) measured two candidate causes on the two-turn music dialogue. «poné una canción» → «Bad Bunny»: the App's arguments stage sends the answer alone, `_ground_explicit_arguments` abstains on a bare name and the model's extraction decided the turn, which asked «¿Qué buscas en YouTube sobre Bad Bunny?» instead of playing. Now media.play.youtube and media.play.query ground on the completed music request that the decision already read (`_completed_missing_music_request` over the history antecedent), so «Bad Bunny», «lofi» or «música clásica» become the query with the person's own words; a negation, a question or an unrelated antecedent still abstain. «poneme una canción» → «algo de jazz»: the playback was verified but the observed title carried «[11.Larga Vida al Rey]» and the composer's template-hole veto rejected every final; `_bracket_is_observed` exempts a bracketed segment that is observed text, while «[hora actual]» stays a hole.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


